WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.560
If a tap fills a tank in ten minutes, then each minute

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.390
it fills one tenth of the tank.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.860
Turning a time into an amount per minute is

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.590
the key move.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.890
Amounts per minute can be added together.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:12.130
Times cannot.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.630
When two taps run together at constant rates,

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.050
the tank fills faster.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.950
The two amounts filled in one minute can be added.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.220
That combined amount per minute tells us how long the

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.310
whole job will take.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.210
One tap fills a tank in six minutes.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.190
Another fills it in three minutes.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.130
Both run at constant rates.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.010
How long do they take together?

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.250
Pause and work out what each tap does in one minute.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.420
Picture the tank in six equal slices.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.940
In one minute, the slow tap fills one slice.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.320
The fast tap fills the whole tank in three minutes,

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.500
so it fills two slices a minute.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.180
Together they fill three slices a minute.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.560
Six slices at three slices a minute takes two minutes.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:01.570
Together the taps take two minutes, which is less than

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.320
either alone, as it should be.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.130
Rates can also work against each other.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.260
A tap fills a tank in four minutes, while a leak would

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.230
empty it in twelve.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.660
In a tank of twelve slices, the tap adds three slices a

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.490
minute and the leak removes one.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.000
The net gain is two slices a minute, so the tank fills

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:20.950
in six minutes.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.440
Moving objects follow the same rule.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:27.770
Two runners start one hundred metres apart and run

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:31.050
towards each other, at six metres per second and four

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.060
metres per second.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.780
The gap closes at ten metres per second.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.560
They meet after ten seconds.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.640
Convert each time into a rate.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.200
Use the same time unit for each rate.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:45.200
Add rates that help and subtract rates that hinder.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.820
Divide the job by the combined rate.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.630
Notebook challenge: one painter paints a fence in four

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.680
hours, another in twelve hours.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:55.540
How long do they take together?
